    "description": "Puget Energy is the holding company for Puget Sound Energy, Washington's regulated electric and gas utility. The utility serves approximately 1.2 million electric customers and 900,000 natural gas customers across a 6,000-square-mile service territory in 10 counties. Its operating model is asset-heavy and regulated, with revenue supported by utility rate structures, generation assets, transmission, distribution, and long-lived network infrastructure. AIMCo has held the investment since the 2009 take-private and increased its stake in 2018, while the current public consortium also includes Macquarie, Ontario Teachers', OMERS, BCI, and PGGM. BCI's 2024 I&RR financial statements disclose a 20.9% ownership interest in Puget Sound Energy, and BCI continued to describe PSE as one of its largest and longest-standing infrastructure investments in 2025.",
